{%- comment -%}
  Is this product one that must not be added to the bag in one click?

  Outputs the string "true" for a restricted product and nothing otherwise, so
  callers capture it:

    {%- capture restricted -%}{%- render 'product-restricted', product: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if restricted == 'true' -%} ... link to the PDP ... {%- endif -%}

  The tag is set in Brand settings (Pharmacy > Restricted product tag) so the
  rule lives in one place. Matching is case-insensitive and exact per tag —
  "Pharmacist-Only" matches, "pharmacist-only-note" does not. A merchant who
  capitalises a tag differently in admin should not silently open the gate,
  and a partial match should not silently close it on an unrelated product.

  IMPORTANT — this is a suppression, not a suitability check. It stops the
  one-click add surfaces (listings, search, recommendations) from bypassing
  the product page. It does NOT ask the customer anything, and the product
  page's own Add to bag still works unconditionally. The questionnaire the
  collection FAQ copy describes does not exist in this theme.

  Accepts: product (required)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign gate_tag = settings.restricted_tag | strip | downcase
  if gate_tag != blank
    assign product_tags = product.tags | join: '||' | downcase | split: '||'
    if product_tags contains gate_tag
      echo 'true'
    endif
  endif
-%}
